WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.235
There are so many new beauty releases

00:00:02.235 --> 00:00:03.403
happening all the time,

00:00:03.403 --> 00:00:05.505
so we gathered some of
the most-hyped products

00:00:05.505 --> 00:00:07.073
to test for ourselves.

00:00:07.073 --> 00:00:10.577
This is the Super Saturated
serum from Experiment.

00:00:10.577 --> 00:00:12.512
It has 30% glycerin in it,

00:00:12.512 --> 00:00:14.881
which I think is what makes it so sticky.

00:00:14.881 --> 00:00:17.183
This is supposed to be a hydrating serum,

00:00:17.183 --> 00:00:19.686
but I'm going to be using
it as a makeup primer.

00:00:19.686 --> 00:00:23.156
It reminds me so much of all
those sticky, tacky primers

00:00:23.156 --> 00:00:25.325
on the market right now,
like the one from Milk.

00:00:25.325 --> 00:00:27.494
This actually felt amazing on my skin.

00:00:27.494 --> 00:00:30.730
It's kind of slimy, but it
just feels so hydrating.

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:33.633
I let it sit for a bit before
applying my foundation on top,

00:00:33.633 --> 00:00:35.869
and everything went on really nicely.

00:00:35.869 --> 00:00:38.972
It's so similar to other
sticky primers I've tried,

00:00:38.972 --> 00:00:41.174
but this is more of a skincare product.

00:00:41.174 --> 00:00:43.877
I'm definitely going to keep
using this as a primer, though.

00:00:43.877 --> 00:00:46.679
I don't know how, but I
managed to get my hands

00:00:46.679 --> 00:00:49.649
on the One/Size blush
trio in Attention Seeker.

00:00:49.649 --> 00:00:52.786
It has a cream, a matte
powder, and a sheen powder.

00:00:52.786 --> 00:00:55.288
I've reviewed these
before and did love them,

00:00:55.288 --> 00:00:58.291
but the cream in this one is just not it.

00:00:58.291 --> 00:01:00.560
It's so chalky and ashy looking.

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:02.095
I get that not every color

00:01:02.095 --> 00:01:04.064
is going to work for every skin tone,

00:01:04.064 --> 00:01:06.499
but the creams in the
other colors I've tried

00:01:06.499 --> 00:01:09.369
were much more true to how
they looked in the pan.

00:01:09.369 --> 00:01:11.404
The matte powder blush is really pretty.

00:01:11.404 --> 00:01:13.506
Combining the matte blush
with the cream blush

00:01:13.506 --> 00:01:15.775
gave me such a better color payoff,

00:01:15.775 --> 00:01:18.511
but the sheen powder is the
real star of the show here.

00:01:18.511 --> 00:01:20.747
It has a bunch of pink, baby blue,

00:01:20.747 --> 00:01:24.317
and lavender shimmer in it
that just looks so beautiful.

00:01:24.317 --> 00:01:26.052
I had to put this on my eyes too.

00:01:26.052 --> 00:01:28.054
I loved it so much.

00:01:28.054 --> 00:01:31.257
This is the Iconic London
Rollaway Glow highlighter.

00:01:31.257 --> 00:01:33.593
It's literally a roll-on highlighter.

00:01:33.593 --> 00:01:34.828
When I first applied it,

00:01:34.828 --> 00:01:37.297
I did go over already-powdered makeup

00:01:37.297 --> 00:01:41.134
and realized that this stuff
dries down almost immediately.

00:01:41.134 --> 00:01:43.203
Like, it simply would not blend.

00:01:43.203 --> 00:01:46.005
So I tried it again over
not-powdered makeup.

00:01:46.005 --> 00:01:47.607
I worked section by section,

00:01:47.607 --> 00:01:49.976
and I also tried to
move at lightning speed,

00:01:49.976 --> 00:01:51.644
and I had a much better outcome.

00:01:51.644 --> 00:01:54.280
I feel like it still dried down so fast.

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:57.217
I had to blend for a while to
get it to look how I wanted,

00:01:57.217 --> 00:01:59.719
but I do think it's very pretty and glowy.

00:01:59.719 --> 00:02:01.988
Fenty Beauty released another lip product.

00:02:01.988 --> 00:02:04.691
This is the Icon velvet liquid lipstick.

00:02:04.691 --> 00:02:06.993
The packaging is so cool.

00:02:06.993 --> 00:02:09.129
Look at this little floating logo.

00:02:09.129 --> 00:02:11.731
The formula is this super-mousse-y cream.

00:02:11.731 --> 00:02:14.901
It doesn't dry down like a
regular liquid lipstick would.

00:02:14.901 --> 00:02:18.238
It just stays this soft
matte finish on the lips.

00:02:18.238 --> 00:02:19.672
These are really pigmented.

00:02:19.672 --> 00:02:21.574
Like, the color is so rich,

00:02:21.574 --> 00:02:24.978
and they feel so comfortable
and pillowy on the lips.

00:02:24.978 --> 00:02:27.413
I've seen people say that
these transfer a lot.

00:02:27.413 --> 00:02:29.582
They're not described
as being transfer-proof,

00:02:29.582 --> 00:02:31.117
but I do see how this formula

00:02:31.117 --> 00:02:32.886
could move around throughout the day.

00:02:32.886 --> 00:02:35.421
I think a good lip liner and
some blotting could help.

00:02:35.421 --> 00:02:36.756
But honestly, I really like

00:02:36.756 --> 00:02:39.092
how this formula feels and looks.

00:02:39.092 --> 00:02:41.861
I have two very similar
products to compare,

00:02:41.861 --> 00:02:44.430
the Essence What a Tint lip and cheek tint

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:45.965
and the Benefit Benetint.

00:02:45.965 --> 00:02:48.468
Both are this watery pink lip stain

00:02:48.468 --> 00:02:50.403
that you can also use on the cheeks,

00:02:50.403 --> 00:02:53.373
but the Essence one is
just way more affordable.

00:02:53.373 --> 00:02:55.875
I have to say I didn't
really like either of these

00:02:55.875 --> 00:02:57.277
on top of foundation.

00:02:57.277 --> 00:03:00.013
I feel like they both
lifted my foundation a bit

00:03:00.013 --> 00:03:01.781
and looked a little patchy.

00:03:01.781 --> 00:03:04.517
The Benetint did have a
better color payoff, though.

00:03:04.517 --> 00:03:05.518
But then on the lips,

00:03:05.518 --> 00:03:07.787
I feel like the Essence
one was more pigmented.

00:03:07.787 --> 00:03:09.255
It was very confusing.

00:03:09.255 --> 00:03:11.424
Both looked patchy on my lips as well.

00:03:11.424 --> 00:03:13.026
They are similar enough, though,

00:03:13.026 --> 00:03:16.196
that you could save the money
and go for the Essence one.

00:03:16.196 --> 00:03:19.999
This is the Make Up for
Ever HD Skin matte velvet

00:03:19.999 --> 00:03:23.937
undetectable longwear
blurring powder foundation.

00:03:23.937 --> 00:03:25.171
These names, you guys.

00:03:25.171 --> 00:03:27.040
They're just getting longer and longer.

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:29.442
I'm always a little scared
of powder foundations

00:03:29.442 --> 00:03:30.510
because I feel like they tend

00:03:30.510 --> 00:03:32.712
to grab on to dryness and texture,

00:03:32.712 --> 00:03:35.682
but I was completely blown away by this.

00:03:35.682 --> 00:03:39.285
This powder is silky
smooth and just glides on.

00:03:39.285 --> 00:03:41.421
I don't understand how they
got a powder foundation

00:03:41.421 --> 00:03:43.122
to look this natural on the skin.

00:03:43.122 --> 00:03:45.191
Ugh, it's just so beautiful!

00:03:45.191 --> 00:03:47.694
And it smoothed out all my problem areas.

00:03:47.694 --> 00:03:49.562
The coverage is also buildable.

00:03:49.562 --> 00:03:51.864
My other makeup went on
top of this really nicely.

00:03:51.864 --> 00:03:53.866
I even did concealer over the powder,

00:03:53.866 --> 00:03:55.435
and it blended out just fine.

00:03:55.435 --> 00:03:56.836
This is a new favorite for me.

00:03:56.836 --> 00:04:00.340
This is the Kaja Jelly Charm
glazed lip stain and blush.

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:02.742
It comes with this supercute key chain.

00:04:02.742 --> 00:04:05.812
This feels really nice
and hydrating on the lips,

00:04:05.812 --> 00:04:07.981
but I don't think it has
a great color payoff.

00:04:07.981 --> 00:04:11.117
The stain it leaves behind
is also pretty subtle.

00:04:11.117 --> 00:04:13.086
I don't think this is a
serious cheek product.

00:04:13.086 --> 00:04:15.388
It's almost, like, too
glossy to be a blush,

00:04:15.388 --> 00:04:18.524
and it lifted a lot of the
product I already had on.

00:04:18.524 --> 00:04:21.594
MAC just released this
Locked Kiss Ink lipstick.

00:04:21.594 --> 00:04:23.930
It's a transfer-proof
and waterproof lipstick

00:04:23.930 --> 00:04:26.299
that's meant to last a really long time.

00:04:26.299 --> 00:04:29.502
The actual formula is more
watery than I was expecting.

00:04:29.502 --> 00:04:32.472
It's on the thinner side and
does need some time to dry

00:04:32.472 --> 00:04:33.873
if you need to add more.

00:04:33.873 --> 00:04:36.442
It's very lightweight and not drying,

00:04:36.442 --> 00:04:37.777
even though it is matte.

00:04:37.777 --> 00:04:39.379
I wore this for about six hours.

00:04:39.379 --> 00:04:40.446
I drank and ate,

00:04:40.446 --> 00:04:42.548
and it still looked good
at the end of the day.

00:04:42.548 --> 00:04:46.052
I also did a kiss test on the
back of my hand and on my dog,

00:04:46.052 --> 00:04:48.521
and I definitely think
this is transfer-proof.

00:04:48.521 --> 00:04:50.990
I'm seeing formulas like
this everywhere nowadays,

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:53.359
so this isn't really
special, but it does work.

00:04:53.359 --> 00:04:55.695
I think the Patrick Ta
Major Glow highlighting mist

00:04:55.695 --> 00:04:56.963
was one of the first products

00:04:56.963 --> 00:04:58.464
to ever be released by the brand,

00:04:58.464 --> 00:04:59.666
but I've never tried it.

00:04:59.666 --> 00:05:01.801
This is essentially a
highlighter in a can.

00:05:01.801 --> 00:05:03.870
I got the duo, which
comes with a mini mist

00:05:03.870 --> 00:05:07.040
and this fan to help you get
a more precise application.

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:09.542
I do think the glow
this gives is beautiful,

00:05:09.542 --> 00:05:11.577
but it's obviously hard to control a mist,

00:05:11.577 --> 00:05:12.645
even with the fan,

00:05:12.645 --> 00:05:15.515
so I ended up getting
highlighter in a lot of places.

00:05:15.515 --> 00:05:18.217
For now, I can see myself using
this as a body highlighter.

00:05:18.217 --> 00:05:20.453
I still need more practice
with it on the face,

00:05:20.453 --> 00:05:22.422
but I do like how it looks on the skin.

00:05:22.422 --> 00:05:24.090
I've used a few of the Rare Beauty

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:25.992
Soft Pinch liquid blushes before,

00:05:25.992 --> 00:05:27.660
but only the matte formulas,

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:29.929
and I've never used a shade this vibrant.

00:05:29.929 --> 00:05:32.899
This is the color Lucky,
and it's a dewy hot pink.

00:05:32.899 --> 00:05:34.500
I actually found this dewy formula

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:36.169
to be a little bit easier to work with

00:05:36.169 --> 00:05:38.471
because it doesn't dry down as fast.

00:05:38.471 --> 00:05:41.207
This product in general needs
a bit of trial and error.

00:05:41.207 --> 00:05:43.009
For me, the easiest way to work with it

00:05:43.009 --> 00:05:45.178
is to apply some on the back of my hand,

00:05:45.178 --> 00:05:46.312
blend that with a sponge,

00:05:46.312 --> 00:05:48.548
and then gently tap it onto the face.

00:05:48.548 --> 00:05:50.650
It does layer nicely over other products,

00:05:50.650 --> 00:05:52.485
and you can pick your level of intensity

00:05:52.485 --> 00:05:55.555
as long as you don't
immediately go in with too much.

00:05:55.555 --> 00:05:57.657
This is one of those colors
that I can see working

00:05:57.657 --> 00:05:58.758
for so many people,

00:05:58.758 --> 00:06:01.160
and I actually think I
prefer the dewy formula.

00:06:01.160 --> 00:06:04.497
This is the Makeup by Mario
MoistureGlow plumping lip color.

00:06:04.497 --> 00:06:06.833
It's supposed to be
full coverage, plumping,

00:06:06.833 --> 00:06:08.501
and weightless on the lips.

00:06:08.501 --> 00:06:10.970
I would say it's one
of those three things.

00:06:10.970 --> 00:06:14.073
It is super moisturizing
and feels good on the lips,

00:06:14.073 --> 00:06:16.976
but unfortunately, the
coverage was really streaky.

00:06:16.976 --> 00:06:18.211
I had to do a couple layers

00:06:18.211 --> 00:06:19.712
to give me the coverage I wanted.

00:06:19.712 --> 00:06:22.181
It was settling a little bit in my lines.

00:06:22.181 --> 00:06:25.218
I also didn't see or
feel any plumping effect.

00:06:25.218 --> 00:06:27.286
I do want to try a more nude shade

00:06:27.286 --> 00:06:28.721
to see if those are any better,

00:06:28.721 --> 00:06:31.758
but for right now, I think
this is just an OK lip gloss.

00:06:31.758 --> 00:06:32.925
This is the Glow Recipe

00:06:32.925 --> 00:06:35.928
strawberry BHA pore-smooth Blur Drops.

00:06:35.928 --> 00:06:38.398
You can use this as a serum or a primer.

00:06:38.398 --> 00:06:39.365
On my bare skin,

00:06:39.365 --> 00:06:41.067
I can definitely see some blurring,

00:06:41.067 --> 00:06:42.935
especially in the area by my nose

00:06:42.935 --> 00:06:45.371
where I feel like I have
the most visible pores.

00:06:45.371 --> 00:06:48.508
However, as a primer,
I absolutely hate this.

00:06:48.508 --> 00:06:50.343
I used products I know work well

00:06:50.343 --> 00:06:52.178
and look great every single time.

00:06:52.178 --> 00:06:53.413
But on top of this primer,

00:06:53.413 --> 00:06:55.314
everything was just looking bad.

00:06:55.314 --> 00:06:56.883
My makeup was so patchy,

00:06:56.883 --> 00:06:58.751
and it made my products pill up.

00:06:58.751 --> 00:07:01.421
I can see myself using this
to help me control my oil

00:07:01.421 --> 00:07:02.555
on my no-makeup days,

00:07:02.555 --> 00:07:04.857
but as a primer, absolutely not.

00:07:04.857 --> 00:07:08.594
I've been seeing these "angel
wing" lashes all over TikTok

00:07:08.594 --> 00:07:10.163
and really wanted to try them.

00:07:10.163 --> 00:07:12.131
If you've ever seen me apply fake lashes,

00:07:12.131 --> 00:07:13.599
you know I'm terrible at it.

00:07:13.599 --> 00:07:15.668
But this style is so cute to me.

00:07:15.668 --> 00:07:17.537
It's very Disney princess.

00:07:17.537 --> 00:07:19.972
I don't particularly
like this brand of lash

00:07:19.972 --> 00:07:22.408
because the band was
just too thick and stiff,

00:07:22.408 --> 00:07:24.410
but I do like the lash style.

00:07:24.410 --> 00:07:25.578
Too Faced came out with these

00:07:25.578 --> 00:07:29.182
Lip Injection Extreme Lip
Shaper plumping lip liners.

00:07:29.182 --> 00:07:30.016
I'm actually a fan

00:07:30.016 --> 00:07:32.585
of their Lip Injection
Extreme Lip Plumpers.

00:07:32.585 --> 00:07:35.254
It does have a pretty
intense tingly feeling,

00:07:35.254 --> 00:07:38.424
just like the plumpers,
but I really enjoyed these.

00:07:38.424 --> 00:07:40.960
They work exactly the same
as the regular plumpers,

00:07:40.960 --> 00:07:42.495
except I think these are better.

00:07:42.495 --> 00:07:45.097
With lip plumpers, you're
supposed to apply a little bit

00:07:45.097 --> 00:07:47.600
outside of your lip line
for a plumping effect.

00:07:47.600 --> 00:07:49.502
And since these are plumping lip liners,

00:07:49.502 --> 00:07:51.170
it just makes it so easy.

00:07:51.170 --> 00:07:54.006
I like that you can define
and plump at the same time.

00:07:54.006 --> 00:07:55.541
I'm holding on to these for sure.

00:07:55.541 --> 00:07:57.043
This is the NYX Face Freezie

00:07:57.043 --> 00:07:59.745
cooling hydration moisturizer and primer.

00:07:59.745 --> 00:08:02.682
It has this really
interesting gel texture.

00:08:02.682 --> 00:08:05.084
I typically don't like primers like this,

00:08:05.084 --> 00:08:07.019
but it blended into my skin quickly

00:08:07.019 --> 00:08:09.422
and it definitely
blurred some of my pores.

00:08:09.422 --> 00:08:11.991
It has a cooling effect
that feels really good.

00:08:11.991 --> 00:08:14.560
I thought I would have an
issue applying my other makeup

00:08:14.560 --> 00:08:16.062
on top of a primer like this,

00:08:16.062 --> 00:08:18.598
but I actually loved how my makeup looked.

00:08:18.598 --> 00:08:21.267
Everything blended out
easily and looked so smooth.

00:08:21.267 --> 00:08:24.036
I don't think I would use this
as an everyday moisturizer,

00:08:24.036 --> 00:08:25.872
but I do like this as a primer.

00:08:25.872 --> 00:08:27.039
I've used the Maybelline

00:08:27.039 --> 00:08:29.442
Instant Age Rewind Eraser for years,

00:08:29.442 --> 00:08:32.512
but never in this pink shade
that recently went viral.

00:08:32.512 --> 00:08:34.747
This is the shade 160 Brightener.

00:08:34.747 --> 00:08:37.450
I just put a bit under each
eye before my concealer.

00:08:37.450 --> 00:08:39.318
The second I started blending it out,

00:08:39.318 --> 00:08:41.420
it brightened so much.

00:08:41.420 --> 00:08:43.723
Next time, I think I would
go in with a little less

00:08:43.723 --> 00:08:45.958
because it's an intense brightener,

00:08:45.958 --> 00:08:47.159
but I think it looked OK

00:08:47.159 --> 00:08:49.262
once I applied my concealer on top.

00:08:49.262 --> 00:08:52.365
The Instant Age Rewind formula
has always been really good.

00:08:52.365 --> 00:08:54.567
My concealer always creases eventually

00:08:54.567 --> 00:08:56.235
because I have a lot of lines,

00:08:56.235 --> 00:09:00.039
but once this concealer dries,
my creasing is so minimal.

00:09:00.039 --> 00:09:01.307
It also had great coverage,

00:09:01.307 --> 00:09:03.242
even before I applied my concealer.

00:09:03.242 --> 00:09:05.211
This is the new Milk Makeup Pore Eclipse

00:09:05.211 --> 00:09:07.480
mattifying and blurring setting spray.

00:09:07.480 --> 00:09:09.849
It's supposed to give
you a soft-focus finish

00:09:09.849 --> 00:09:11.050
and control oil,

00:09:11.050 --> 00:09:13.319
something I definitely need help with.

00:09:13.319 --> 00:09:14.687
I really like the mist on this.

00:09:14.687 --> 00:09:15.755
It's super fine.

00:09:15.755 --> 00:09:18.424
I feel like I noticed a soft-focus effect

00:09:18.424 --> 00:09:19.792
after setting my makeup.

00:09:19.792 --> 00:09:21.961
It is a little too matte-looking for me.

00:09:21.961 --> 00:09:23.563
I like a little bit of dewiness.

00:09:23.563 --> 00:09:26.532
But it didn't make my
makeup look dry or crusty.

00:09:26.532 --> 00:09:28.434
I did a check-in about five hours later

00:09:28.434 --> 00:09:29.769
and was actually really impressed

00:09:29.769 --> 00:09:31.437
with how it controlled my oil.

00:09:31.437 --> 00:09:33.906
My nose and my forehead
are usually so oily

00:09:33.906 --> 00:09:36.042
within a few hours, but
I still looked matte

00:09:36.042 --> 00:09:38.611
and all of the makeup was
still visible on my face.

